THE CAR SIDE, ON THE SAME BENCH SESSION
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CAR: Freenove ESP32-S3-WROOM CAM (OpenBot, DIY_ESP32 body), USB-UART bridge CH343 on COM4.

  .tools\arduino.cmd compile -u -p COM4 --fqbn "esp32:esp32:esp32s3:PartitionScheme=huge_app" OpenBot/firmware/openbot

1. THE FIRST CAR BUILD RESET-LOOPED, AND ITS OWN DRIVER SAID WHY

    r
    Waiting a client connection to notify...
    E (824) wifi:Error! Should enable WiFi modem sleep when both WiFi and Bluetooth are enabled!!!!!!
    abort() was called at PC 0x420bec47 on core 0
    Backtrace: 0x403779c6:0x3fcb6730 0x4037fb71:0x3fcb6750 ...
    Rebooting...

   A real bug in the ESP-NOW addition, not a power problem: the car runs BLE for the phone app as well,
   and esp_wifi_set_ps(WIFI_PS_NONE) - which the badge can afford, having no BLE - is forbidden when
   both radios are enabled. The driver aborts inside esp_wifi_start(), so the car reset-looped and the
   badge's link never came up. Fixed by setting modem sleep (WIFI_PS_MIN_MODEM) on the car only;
   esp_now.h notes that with no wake window configured the station stays awake while ESP-NOW is in use,
   so the receiver still hears the badge.

2. AFTER THE FIX: CLEAN BOOT, BOTH RADIOS UP

    Waiting a client connection to notify...
    ESP-NOW ready: channel 1, pair key 0x5A17BAD6
    ------------------
    Voltage:    N/A
    Left RPM:  N/A
    Right RPM:  N/A
    Distance:   N/A
    ------------------

   Over 16 seconds: 0 aborts, 0 reboots, the BLE advertising line still present (the phone path is
   intact), and the once-a-second vehicle report running. Voltage/RPM/Distance are N/A because this
   body has no sensors fitted - it is the sonar/encoder-free DIY_ESP32 build.

   No badge was transmitting during the capture ("badge paired" never appeared): the badge was not on
   USB, and the image it is holding is the dongle-safe one, which does not start the radio at boot.

